{"text": "EDUCATION:\n\nEXPERIENCE:\n\n00329486\n16586884yv.1\n\nJUAN D. REYES, III, Esq.\n(b) (6)\n\nQuinnipiac College School of Law, Hamden, C.T.\nJuris Doctor, May 1995\nHonors: Bridgeport Law School Scholar recipient, 1992\nActivities: International Law Society\n\nEmory University, Atlanta, G.A.\nBachelor of Arts in Political Science, May 1990\nMinor Concentration in English Literature\nActivities: Alpha Tau Omega Fraternity- Alumni Representative, Spring 1989;\nEmory Rugby Club; Circle K Club- Volunteer for Community Services; Varsity Track Team\n\nBrowning School, New York, N.Y. - Graduated May 1986\nActivities: (6)\n\nSeyfarth Shaw New York, N.Y Jan 2013-Present\nPartner\nPartner in one of the largest international real estate groups in the United States specializing in all aspects of\nland use and development law. Extensive knowledge in zoning, planning, landmarks and building code\nmatters. Counsels an array of clients involving regulatory and discretionary governmental approval\n\nReed Smith, New York, N.Y Jan 2010-Dec 2012\nPartner\nPartner in an international real estate group specializing in all aspects of land use and development law.\nExtensive knowledge in zoning, planning, landmarks and building code matters.\nCounsels an array of clients involving regulatory and discretionary governmental approval\n\nRiker, Danzig, Scherer, Hyland, Perretti, New York, N.Y Nov 2007-Dec 2009\nPartner\nPartner in New York and New Jersey real estate group specializing in all aspects of land use and development\nlaw. Extensive knowledge in zoning, planning, landmarks and building code matters.\nCounsels an array of clients involving regulatory and discretionary governmental approvals.\n\nHartman & Craven, New York, N.Y Nov 2005-Nov 2007\nPartner\nPartner in New York City based real estate group specializing in all aspects of land use and development law.\nExtensive knowledge in zoning, planning, landmarks and building code matters.\nCounsels an array of clients involving regulatory and discretionary governmental approvals.\n\nDavidoff , Malito, & Hutcher, New York, N.Y. May 2002-Nov 2005\nSenior Associate\nSpecialized in governmental practice, with particular emphasis on land use law.\nCounseled array of clients in matters involving regulatory and discretionary approvals.\nSignificant experience in the interpretation and application of law, administrative\ncodes and zoning regulations.\n\nNew York City Board of Standards and Appeals, New York, N.Y. Oct 2000-May 2002\nGeneral Counsel\nResearched and drafted legal memoranda and formal resolutions. Advised Board on laws\nrelating to zoning, construction and administrative procedure. Advised Board on\nconducting public hearings. Oversaw legal unit. Coordinated with New York City\nLaw Department for outside litigation. The Board of Standards and Appeals is a\nquasi-judicial component of the City\u2019s land use regulations, development and construction.\nThe Board has the power to interpret the meaning or applicability of the New York City\nZoning Resolution, the Building and Fire Codes and Multiple Dwelling Law. The Board\ncan grant variances, appeals, and special permits under the City Charter.",
